You are assisting in building a full-scale Climate Change Data Analysis platform.
Your tasks include data engineering, machine learning, visualization, and website development.
Follow all requirements below and generate production-quality code, structure, and documentation.

📌 PROJECT DESCRIPTION

Build an end-to-end analytics system that analyzes long-term climate change indicators such as:

Global temperature anomalies

CO₂ atmospheric concentrations

Methane (CH₄) levels

Global sea level rise

The system should identify trends, correlations, anomalies, and perform predictive analysis for future climate conditions.

📌 CORE REQUIREMENTS

Copilot should generate:

🔹 1. Project Structure (Full Repository)

Create a complete project layout:

/data/raw
/data/processed
/data/sample (100-row dataset)
/pipeline/ingestion
/pipeline/transformation
/pipeline/ml
/notebooks
/visualizations
/dashboard
/website
/docs

🔹 2. Data Engineering Pipeline

Build reusable pipeline scripts for:

Ingestion

Pull NASA GISS, NOAA temperature datasets

Pull NOAA greenhouse gas CO₂ & CH₄ datasets

Pull NOAA/NASA sea level datasets

Simulate ingestion using Kafka & Airflow DAGs

Store data in HDFS or AWS S3 bucket format

Transformation

Data cleaning with Pandas

Schema standardization

Feature engineering

Time-series alignment

Merge datasets by year or month

Outlier detection

Output

Store cleaned datasets in /data/processed

🔹 3. Machine Learning

Generate Python scripts & notebooks for:

Trend estimation (linear regression, moving avg)

Time-series forecasting (ARIMA / Prophet)

Multivariate correlation analysis

CO₂ vs temperature correlation models

Sea-level prediction models

Save models under /pipeline/ml/models.

🔹 4. Visualizations

Generate code for:

Line charts of temperature anomalies

CO₂ growth over decades

Sea-level rise graphs

Methane rise

Heatmap correlation matrix

Use Matplotlib / Plotly (no seaborn unless necessary).

🔹 5. Sample Dataset (100 Rows)

Generate a synthetic dataset with:

year, global_temp_anomaly, co2_ppm, methane_ppb, sea_level_mm


Store as /data/sample/climate_sample.csv.

🔹 6. Dashboard

Create dashboards using:

Tableau or Power BI

Provide exported .twbx or .pbix instructions

Provide SQL/data model used for the dashboard

Also generate:

Summary KPIs

Trend cards

Maps (if possible)

🔹 7. Modern Website UI

Create a complete gradient-based website (HTML/CSS + optional JS):

Sections:

Landing page

Datasets

Pipeline architecture

Visualizations gallery

ML predictions

Download dataset

Contact/info

Design requirements:

Gradient backgrounds

Glassmorphism cards

Smooth fade/slide animations

High-contrast typography

Responsive mobile-first layout

🔹 8. Documentation

Generate:

README.md (comprehensive)

Architecture diagram (Mermaid + PNG version)

System workflow explanation

APIs and dependencies

Setup instructions

Using the pipeline

Using dashboards

📌 SPECIAL INSTRUCTIONS

Write clean, modular, production-ready code

Add comments, docstrings, and typing hints

Use best ML/data engineering practices

When generating code, create full files, not fragments

When generating DAGs, include full imports

When generating HTML/CSS, include full pages

Use realistic sample values in the synthetic dataset

📌 FINAL ACTION

Start by generating the full repo structure and placeholder files.
Then proceed step-by-step through ingestion → transformation → ML → visualizations → website → documentation.